{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/martinring/tmlanguage/master/tmlanguage.json",
  "scopeName": "streamlord.kotlin.injection",
  "injectionSelector": "L:source.kotlin -comment -string -meta.dsl-file.streamlord",
  "patterns": [
    {
      "include": "#dsl-file"
    },
    {
      "include": "#attributes-index"
    },
    {
      "include": "#html-call"
    },
    {
      "include": "#script-call"
    },
    {
      "include": "#html-string"
    }
  ],
  "repository": {
    "dsl-file": {
      "comment": "From the DSL's import, or its own package, to the end of the file: a file calls the DSL's top-level functions only through one, so only there are its calls Streamlord's. The region adds a scope and Kotlin's grammar inside it, nothing else; streamlord.kotlin.dsl.injection colours the calls in it, at any depth, and this grammar stays out of it so it does not open again.",
      "name": "meta.dsl-file.streamlord",
      "begin": "^(?=[ \\t]*(?:import[ \\t]+io\\.github\\.markusaugust\\.streamlord\\.html\\.|package[ \\t]+io\\.github\\.markusaugust\\.streamlord\\.html(?![\\p{L}\\p{Nd}_])))",
      "end": "(?!)",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "source.kotlin"
        }
      ]
    },
    "attributes-index": {
      "comment": "kotlinx.html's own way to write an attribute, attributes[\"data-on:click\"] = \"...\": Datastar in every file, for the catalog's attributes only, the check after the name keeping data-on-intersects out; grammar.test.ts holds both lists to the catalog. The name in the key as an attribute name. A literal assigned to an attribute that takes an expression is the expression when it is the whole statement, as the diagnostics read it: not the first half of a concatenation, and not a raw string.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "begin": "\\b(attributes)(\\s*\\[\\s*)(\")(data-(?:star-)?(?:custom-validity|on-signal-patch|view-transition|on-intersect|match-media|on-interval|replace-url|on-resize|computed|animate|signals|effect|on-raf|class|style|attr|init|show|text|on)(?=[:\"]|__)[A-Za-z0-9_:.-]*)(\")(\\s*\\])(\\s*)(=)(\\s*\\$*)(\")(?!\"\")(?=(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*\"[ \\t]*(?:[;}]|$))",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            },
            "4": {
              "patterns": [
                {
                  "include": "streamlord.html.injection#attribute-name"
                }
              ]
            },
            "5": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            },
            "8": {
              "name": "keyword.operator.assignment.kotlin"
            },
            "10": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\")",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.inline.datastar",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#kotlin-escapes"
            },
            {
              "include": "source.datastar"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b(attributes)(\\s*\\[\\s*)(\")(data-(?:star-)?(?:on-signal-patch-filter|scroll-into-view|custom-validity|on-signal-patch|view-transition|preserve-attr|ignore-morph|json-signals|on-intersect|query-string|match-media|on-interval|replace-url|indicator|on-resize|computed|animate|persist|signals|effect|ignore|on-raf|class|nonce|style|attr|bind|init|show|text|ref|on)(?=[:\"]|__)[A-Za-z0-9_:.-]*)(\")(\\s*\\])",
          "captures": {
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            },
            "4": {
              "patterns": [
                {
                  "include": "streamlord.html.injection#attribute-name"
                }
              ]
            },
            "5": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "html-string": {
      "comment": "HTML in a string that is not handed to a Streamlord call: a function that returns markup, a val with a fragment. Recognised by its first character, or by IntelliJ's injection marker (@Language(\"HTML\") or // language=HTML) before it.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "comment": "The annotation on a parameter (`@Language(\"HTML\") html: String,`): consumed, reaches nothing.",
          "match": "(@Language\\(\\s*\"(?i:html)\"\\s*\\))(?=\\s*(?:va[lr]\\s+)?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\\s*:)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "storage.type.annotation.kotlin"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "begin": "(@Language\\(\\s*\"(?i:html)\"\\s*\\))",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "storage.type.annotation.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "comment": "The annotation on a function or property: ends after the next triple-quoted literal, or after a double-quoted literal that ends the line (`val x = \"<b>\"`). A double-quoted string before that, such as a parameter default, is a plain string.",
          "end": "(?<=\"\"\")|(?<=\")\\s*$",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#html-triple-string"
            },
            {
              "include": "#html-double-string"
            },
            {
              "include": "#plain-double-string"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "begin": "(//\\s*language=(?i:html)\\b[^\\n]*)",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "comment.line.double-slash.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "end": "(?<=\"\"\")|(?<=\")\\s*$",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#html-triple-string"
            },
            {
              "include": "#html-double-string"
            },
            {
              "include": "#plain-double-string"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "begin": "(\\$*\"\"\")(?=\\s*<(?:[A-Za-z]|!--|!(?i:doctype)))",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.triple.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\"\"\")",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.triple.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.html",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "match": "\\$\\{'\\$'\\}",
              "name": "constant.character.escape.dollar.kotlin"
            },
            {
              "include": "text.html.basic"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "begin": "(\\$*\")(?=<(?:[A-Za-z]|!--))",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\")",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.html",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#kotlin-escapes"
            },
            {
              "include": "text.html.basic"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "html-triple-string": {
      "begin": "(\\$*\"\"\")",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.triple.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\"\"\")",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.triple.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.html",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "match": "\\$\\{'\\$'\\}",
          "name": "constant.character.escape.dollar.kotlin"
        },
        {
          "include": "text.html.basic"
        }
      ]
    },
    "html-double-string": {
      "comment": "A double-quoted literal that opens with a tag, under an HTML marker: HTML.",
      "begin": "(\\$*\")(?=<(?:[A-Za-z]|!--))",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\")",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.html",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#kotlin-escapes"
        },
        {
          "include": "text.html.basic"
        }
      ]
    },
    "plain-double-string": {
      "comment": "Any other double-quoted literal under an HTML marker, such as a parameter default: a string, nothing more. Listed after html-double-string, which wins at the same quote.",
      "begin": "(\\$*\")",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\")",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "name": "string.quoted.double.kotlin",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#kotlin-escapes"
        }
      ]
    },
    "kotlin-escapes": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "match": "\\\\[\\$\"'\\\\ntbr]|\\\\u[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}",
          "name": "constant.character.escape.kotlin"
        },
        {
          "match": "\\$\\{'\\$'\\}",
          "name": "constant.character.escape.dollar.kotlin"
        }
      ]
    },
    "expression-call-first-arg": {
      "comment": "dataOnClick(\"...\"), dataText(\"...\"), dataInit(\"...\") and friends: the first string is a Datastar expression.",
      "begin": "\\b(dataOnClick|dataOnSubmit|dataOnChange|dataOnInput|dataOnKeydown|dataOnFetch|dataOnIntersect|dataOnInterval|dataOnSignalPatch|dataInit|dataEffect|dataText|dataShow|dataOnRaf|dataOnResize|dataCustomValidity|dataReplaceUrl|dataViewTransition|peek|clipboardExpr)(\\s*\\(\\s*\\$*)(\")(?!\"\")",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "entity.name.function.kotlin"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\")",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "meta.embedded.inline.datastar",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#kotlin-escapes"
        },
        {
          "include": "source.datastar"
        }
      ]
    },
    "expression-call-second-arg": {
      "comment": "dataOn(\"click\", \"...\"), dataComputed(\"name\", \"...\"), dataClass(\"name\", \"...\"): the second string is the expression.",
      "begin": "\\b(dataOn|dataComputed|dataClass|dataStyle|dataAttr|dataSignals|dataAnimate|setExpr)(\\s*\\(\\s*\\$*)(\"[^\"\\n]*\")(\\s*,\\s*\\$*)(\")(?!\"\")",
      "beginCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "entity.name.function.kotlin"
        },
        "3": {
          "name": "string.quoted.double.kotlin"
        },
        "5": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "end": "(\")",
      "endCaptures": {
        "1": {
          "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
        }
      },
      "contentName": "meta.embedded.inline.datastar",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "include": "#kotlin-escapes"
        },
        {
          "include": "source.datastar"
        }
      ]
    },
    "html-call": {
      "comment": "patchElements(\"\"\"<div>...</div>\"\"\") and friends: HTML inside the string.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "begin": "\\b(patchElements|respondElements|datastarElements|PatchElements|ElementsResponse)(\\s*\\(\\s*(?:elements\\s*=\\s*)?\\$*)(\"\"\")",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "entity.name.function.kotlin"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.triple.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\"\"\")",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.triple.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.html",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "match": "\\$\\{'\\$'\\}",
              "name": "constant.character.escape.dollar.kotlin"
            },
            {
              "include": "text.html.basic"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "begin": "\\b(patchElements|respondElements|datastarElements|PatchElements|ElementsResponse)(\\s*\\(\\s*(?:elements\\s*=\\s*)?\\$*)(\")",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "entity.name.function.kotlin"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\")",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.html",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#kotlin-escapes"
            },
            {
              "include": "text.html.basic"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "script-call": {
      "comment": "executeScript(\"\"\"...\"\"\"): JavaScript inside the string.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "begin": "\\b(executeScript|respondScript|datastarScript|ExecuteScript)(\\s*\\(\\s*(?:script\\s*=\\s*)?\\$*)(\"\"\")",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "entity.name.function.kotlin"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.triple.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\"\"\")",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.triple.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.javascript",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "match": "\\$\\{'\\$'\\}",
              "name": "constant.character.escape.dollar.kotlin"
            },
            {
              "include": "source.js"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "begin": "\\b(executeScript|respondScript|datastarScript|ExecuteScript)(\\s*\\(\\s*(?:script\\s*=\\s*)?\\$*)(\")",
          "beginCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "entity.name.function.kotlin"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.begin.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "end": "(\")",
          "endCaptures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "punctuation.definition.string.end.kotlin string.quoted.double.kotlin"
            }
          },
          "contentName": "meta.embedded.block.javascript",
          "patterns": [
            {
              "include": "#kotlin-escapes"
            },
            {
              "include": "source.js"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
